+(duration-type)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. The value is either a whole
+number of seconds, like `90`, or one or more `<integer><unit>` groups using the units `d` (days), `h` (hours), `m`
+(minutes), and `s` (seconds), like `2d` or `1h30m`. Each unit may appear at most once and in that order, without
+spaces. Units are case-insensitive. Negative and fractional values are not accepted.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s", show_default=True)
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds.")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout=1h30m"])
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout=90"])
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout=1.5h"])
+    invoke(wait, args=["--help"])
+```
+
+```{versionadded} 8.5.1
+```
+
